# HELD-FREE-NAME-OTHER-TYPE: a binding of the calling body's own, of
# another numeric type, is converted where the held call stands. h3's n is a
# size_t. The root calls h3 above its own int n, where it has none yet: the
# copy, 1001; and below it: 40, converted, 41. own40 has an int n of 40 and
# calls h3 itself: 41. neg has an int n of -1: the row refuses it, neg's
# implicit `convert`, caught by the root: 9. Entry 7.
fn: make3 (size_t: n) fn: () size_t
    fn: f3 () size_t
        return: n + 1U
    return: f3

@: h3 make3(1000U)

fn: own40 () size_t
    int: n 40
    return: h3()
end: own40

fn: neg () size_t
    int: n -1
    return: h3()
end: neg

size_t: before h3()
int: n 40
size_t: after h3()
size_t: mine own40()
int: r 3
size_t: got 0U
got: neg()
catch: convert ()
    r: 9
int: ok 7
if: before != 1001U || after != 41U || mine != 41U || r != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
